#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124821 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f9ab465-9b60-5926-9caf-66fa38e4437c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448472} {:answer/id #uuid "41ff740e-9971-5305-8cca-6d16b6176274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41ff740e-9971-5305-8cca-6d16b6176274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448473} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e509c73-9172-59d0-a89f-3107e3fd27d0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449276} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "208f176c-8dfc-594d-b8d8-8273c02ccbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448474} {:answer/id #uuid "a82bd6fd-6532-53f7-b93a-eee32c232323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "208f176c-8dfc-594d-b8d8-8273c02ccbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448474} :answer-field/id #uuid "06489517-8558-587b-98d1-a63c1fea14be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0cf8462-0245-553e-8f2f-32ebff1011e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448476} {:answer/id #uuid "34965ccb-0322-5f75-90dc-bd64d3a0a98f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0cf8462-0245-553e-8f2f-32ebff1011e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448476} :answer-field/id #uuid "e666111a-27b4-5617-a072-b9aa01376d65" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5496aa6-8f04-55cb-807e-38886a8c0e30" :question/math-academy-id "q-163722" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈-12+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${a}_{11}=-2$ and $det(A)=-24$\n\n- **II.** $A$ is positive-definite\n\n- **III.** $a$ is a local minimum of $f$" :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, let's recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-2$ and\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}|=-24.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-2<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}|=-24<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a saddle point of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124648 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "233eab4c-ab17-53a8-ae03-f6f28ac78922" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ed3573-aeb0-5cc8-aa92-2d155431b5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "not a critical point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281776} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1c7147-5d4b-5e81-833d-854efd096d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "local maximum" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281777} {:answer/id #uuid "194b6ddb-9926-5f0f-9190-d8ff2af941e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "local minimum" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281919} {:answer/id #uuid "27c2e034-47f4-59cd-b78d-6e4055cb354d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282029} {:answer/id #uuid "b540775c-a7f1-590f-8bcc-78b4486e47c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "inconclusive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a1c7147-5d4b-5e81-833d-854efd096d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "local maximum" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281777} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5a40b87-497b-52fb-93f4-bce3fac9446e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284284}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9c2261a-709f-5777-b889-b197f8b76cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-163773" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}(x-a).\n$$\n\nGiven that the eigenvalues of ${f}^{″}(a)$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ what type of point is $a?$" :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nThe quadratic Taylor expansion of a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{n}$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}{f}^{″}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSince the quadratic Taylor expansion of $f$ has no $(x-a)$ term, we can conclude that ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ Hence, $a$ is a critical point of $f.$\n\nFinally, notice that both the eigenvalues of ${f}^{″}(a)$ are negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & =-1<0 \\\\ {\\lambda }_{2} & =-3<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix is negative definite. Therefore, $a$ is a local maximum of $f.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124648 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "233eab4c-ab17-53a8-ae03-f6f28ac78922" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40769601-5e6b-5811-8d87-d4e245a3b44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "inconclusive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282244} {:answer/id #uuid "697f5a10-56de-5e96-8d49-0b219f74b52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "not a critical point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282594} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc1225a-208e-5576-8fa1-8495783e27ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282909} {:answer/id #uuid "994080d1-474f-5f19-920a-c11b2301f486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "local maximum" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283021} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0fe6f7-98c5-5152-b74a-4001671d9b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "local minimum" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a0fe6f7-98c5-5152-b74a-4001671d9b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "local minimum" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283032} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebbb4b19-fdb5-5b6d-a6cf-ba581d730234" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45b6a4ae-c84e-567c-b717-cd9dbeea1d7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163785" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈1+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}(x-a).\n$$\n\nGiven that the eigenvalues of ${f}^{″}(a)$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=8,{\\lambda }_{2}=3-\\sqrt{2}$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=3+\\sqrt{2},$ what type of point is $a?$" :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nThe quadratic Taylor expansion of a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{n}$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}{f}^{″}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSince the quadratic Taylor expansion of $f$ has no $(x-a)$ term, we can conclude that ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ Hence, $a$ is a critical point of $f.$\n\nFinally, notice that all the eigenvalues of ${f}^{″}(a)$ are positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & =8>0 \\\\ {\\lambda }_{2} & =3-\\sqrt{2}>0 \\\\ {\\lambda }_{3} & =3+\\sqrt{2}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix is positive definite. Therefore, $a$ is a local minimum of $f.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79848729-40e3-58f8-aead-25a4bf9f91ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468960} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf43adb-e00a-52d6-9171-6bb57f6c2393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79848729-40e3-58f8-aead-25a4bf9f91ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468960} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a2e7e84-4d50-5f18-bf38-f3d4119b4f61" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470092} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1aeab25-5623-5fb1-a33c-8659586a7265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468962} {:answer/id #uuid "000a5f85-f437-53f8-913c-2f859328fe33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1aeab25-5623-5fb1-a33c-8659586a7265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468962} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ea7aae1-f019-57b9-9bd5-f09302e71e14" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e948e36-b6c1-5434-958f-e2bbe1ea693a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468964} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6e86d7-eddf-593d-8716-1c788f8c5e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f6e86d7-eddf-593d-8716-1c788f8c5e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468965} :answer-field/id #uuid "431cae4d-364e-588f-aeb2-fee9cea68018" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61ffb698-9cc2-5e02-b6d9-afec7d1f3422" :question/math-academy-id "q-163790" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈-7+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $det(A)>0$\n- **II.** $A$ is positive-definite\n- **III.** $a$ is a local maximum of $f$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, we recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-5(11)-2(-4)+4(10) \\\\  & =-7<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-5<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|=11>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-7<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is negative-definite.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the matrix $A$ is negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local maximum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124647 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0fb118f-c1cc-51fd-a8cc-c29cf705acfe" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Local Extrema of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a548b762-254d-5503-9bdc-ee9b3db0343c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465537} {:answer/id #uuid "5b890428-e714-50e8-a25d-194ffa0fa64a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a548b762-254d-5503-9bdc-ee9b3db0343c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465537} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebd0423b-7a8f-573f-9d6b-7f4e7280a365" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466612} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de59ca97-1aed-5c82-97ae-0036990ece61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465539} {:answer/id #uuid "aba0580e-6d6b-54b7-9354-14b60eb284b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aba0580e-6d6b-54b7-9354-14b60eb284b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465540} :answer-field/id #uuid "24e7a461-81df-553b-9d92-c7e10bc4d0f6" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac0c9d0-2ccc-5127-9770-3602fe1c2d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465541} {:answer/id #uuid "fd97d7fc-8560-50f4-a5ef-982684deaed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ac0c9d0-2ccc-5127-9770-3602fe1c2d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465541} :answer-field/id #uuid "62bb3be7-ac04-517e-97e6-83c3aca76a8c" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9951cfdd-e926-5c89-b9b0-0744d28851f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465543} {:answer/id #uuid "3032c93e-22e6-5f71-81c9-c6bdd88b04e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9951cfdd-e926-5c89-b9b0-0744d28851f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465543} :answer-field/id #uuid "48758690-7815-5e22-aea8-571e2ab0e1ff" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "140468c2-8315-56a7-adfc-2601c4482a06" :question/math-academy-id "q-164150" :question/problem "![](images/fd/fdfae6a5a321d1dbc235d06438847d5a0cc471fa4e31575f36c3967dca239824.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are local minimum points?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f(x,y)$ has a local minimum point at $(a,b)$ if $f(x,y)\\ge f(a,b)$ for all points $(x,y)$ in a neighborhood of $(a,b).$ \n\nIn other words, we can take a neighborhood of $(x,y)$-values such that the point $(x,y,f(x,y))$ is the lowest point on the graph in the neighborhood.\n\nSuch neighborhood exists for the point $B.$ Hence, $B$ is a local minimum.\n\n![](images/82/82291f89bd32f3a3a20d39dfc89de91b2f673bec7c802cebf6d5fa3b4136ace1.png)"}]}
